WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
 I came with an idea and I threw it out as I was listening and looking here.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.490
 I introduced Father Jim O'Donnell here four years ago and him to the back, but

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.000
 I will be next year and the year after that

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
 because what I realized sitting up here today looking around is a good view.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.240
 All these people are all from different races but we're all the ones who have

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.000
 been with us.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
 [applause]

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
 And the person I want to pay my deepest respect to tonight is my mother.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
 As I'm sitting there saying we're a black lady without the example that she set.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.340
 My father got sick with tuberculosis and spent six years in a hospital with

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.000
 some acres.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.000
 We lost our house. We were never afraid because she never had a speech.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.080
 And we ended up in the projects on almost 25th Street and she would say, "Jackie,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.000
 you're the man of the house until today,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.740
 "consult. What does that mean, Mom?" I had no idea. I was seven years old at

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.000
 point six and a half.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.070
 She said, "It means you got to get a job, Jackie. You got to bring some money

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.000
 in the house with that."

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.000
 That's where my career started. Thank God for Mom.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.000
 And I went out and I knocked on doors and I got a big group with two customers.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.140
 And I built that up to three or four and then it paid quick with five and

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.000
 pretty soon I had ten or twelve customers.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.740
 And I had a big group no matter where I was. When my dad got out of the

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.000
 hospital years later,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.090
 we moved out to the airport and a house that fell down after the first

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.000
 sanctuary there,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.740
 the garage collapsed out of my father's car, which was a 20-year-old car at the

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.000
 time.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.320
 And we all happened until he grabbed us in the ears. My brother and I, I think

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:47.000
 that was funny

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.000
 because that was the whole family walk that he had just thrown up.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:57.000
 But the beginnings of all that teaches you to be a family and to work.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.000
 And the money that I made gave to my mother. That was the whole way we did.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.000
 Everybody that got a job, Theresa Baby-Sapp, she gave it to Mom.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.000
 It was family that was going to win. Well, that sort of sunk into me.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.820
 And I started a business later. I worked for a guy. I was the first guy to ever

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.000
 work for this gentleman.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.000
 And he was running an 80,000-hour business.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.330
 Pretty soon, he started cheating me. I walked up to him once and I said, "Mr.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.000
 So-and-so,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.630
 I don't mind that. Please don't do that again because I'm probably not going to

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.000
 work for you."

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.000
 He said, "No." The second time, several months later, he sure did me a hug.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.520
 What I knew I had coming, I just walked in and I said, "So-and-so, I can't do

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.000
 this.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.570
 I can't work for you because I don't trust you and I don't respect you. So I'm

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.000
 quitting."

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.000
 And don't worry about your damn business. I will find something else to do.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.000
 I'm not going to steal this business from you.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.740
 He called me about three or four days later and he says, "Jack, I've had two

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:56.000
 offers for the business.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.000
 I had no idea whether it was true or not."

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.000
 But he says, "It's probably worth more to you than anybody else.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.000
 By this time, I had built this little $80,000 business up to about $7 million."

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
 And he had no clue, you know, where it was coming from.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:18.400
 So I sat down with some bankers, my brother-in-law, Jim Forshey, and Cleveland

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.000
 Trust,

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.000
 and he says, "I want to know the problems before I know the successes

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.000
 so I can help if I ever get to that point."

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.000
 And that's how we started.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:31.250
 And so I'm sitting here tonight looking at all these different people from all

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.000
 these different places

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.000
 that are all now wanting this room being recognized in our city.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:43.000
 And I'm like, "Yeah." It hits me that we all have to be good to one another.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.000
 And as time went by in my business, there wasn't too much time.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.000
 I said, "If Mom did this and we got a nickel on Sunday's ice cream cone,

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.000
 we'd run up to the store and buy nickel ice cream cone."

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.000
 And that was a big day.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.120
 My sister and I would maybe even get a candy bar and spit it and sit down the

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.000
 corner up there.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:07.000
 It was amazing the way you started seeing the things that are important to you.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.000
 And it was about being a family and working together.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.000
 So Mom started sharing when I got to the next step,

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.000
 and I started making success happen at the company we all work.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.000
 I shared the wealth with them.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.000
 30 percent of everything that I made went to the employees.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.210
 So the way we did it, I said, "If we're going to work as hard as we're all

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.000
 going to work,

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.000
 then we're all going to be rewarded for it."

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.000
 And so that was the beginning of our success.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.130
 The bankers, some of the bankers I had said, "Oh, you can't do that. You

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.000
 shouldn't do that."

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.000
 I said, "Well, this is the way we're going to do it."

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.000
 So you have to have a belief in yourself and a belief in other people.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.000
 And if you're going to ask them to work as hard as you are going to work,

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.000
 then you're going to share it with them.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.740
 And that went on for many, many, many years until we sold the company to a big

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.000
 conglomerate.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.000
 And I retired.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.000
 My sons were still there. They bought the company back with another fellow

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.000
 who made our update from the first day I ever walked in there.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.740
 And he still made it in force, and now that's a joint effort between the two of

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.000
 us.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.000
 And the business has still run the same way.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.050
 Everybody in that company that works there but south is part of it, and they

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.000
 just paid for it.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.000
 So I'm proud of my mother.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:27.000
 I'm super proud of my dad and the family that taught me how to be successful.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.000
 And I have something that we're going to change it.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.000
 And I hope it strikes some of you the same way,

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.000
 because you can hear all the so-called experts that come in

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.000
 start telling you how to run a business.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.000
 You can't run fast enough to get away from half of a business.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.000
 They're telling you how to be a customer, how to screw you to voice.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.000
 You can make more money.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.000
 Ask not how you do it. Ask for redemption.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.000
 So everybody here tonight, congratulations.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.000
 It's beautiful to hear these stories.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.000
 And it's beautiful that we're in these families.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.000
 We don't see color, we just see people.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.000
 So congratulations to all of us for being here.

